{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794565988887,"sessionID":"ses_e2b88d3f9ffe7JDxWguwirnDeF","part":{"partID":"prt_1d477dcf0002hdpSSk0chgbM5M","sessionID":"ses_e2b88d3f9ffe7JDxWguwirnDeF","messageID":"msg_1d477a912001MGBfmK8YOZVZQc","type":"tool","id":"call_2af5e1b621404da0b56f1bd0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '83p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"- [x] T003 [P] Report the rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)` and recapture the baseline (`CAP`, `BASE`). Add `const PROMPT_POLICY_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/prompt-policy.js')` beside `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE`, add it to the array the existence loop checks, import `extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions` from it after the `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE` import and add `routeNeedsMode` to that import's names. Before the corpus loop, declare `needsModeRows` as an empty array and `needsModeFloor` as 0. Inside the loop, hold the hub's route as `const route = topId !== undefined && COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS.has(topId) ? readCompiledRoute(workspaceRoot, topId, row.prompt) : undefined` and pass `route` to `attachCommand` where the call reads the route inline today, so the label reuses the same lookup. After the line that sets `delivered`, add `const needsMode = route !== undefined && delivered === undefined && routeNeedsMode(topId, route, extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions(row.prompt))` and push `row.id` into `needsModeRows` when it is true. Inside the `wantsSilence` block, add 1 to `needsModeFloor` when `needsMode` is true. In `attachedMetrics`, right after `attachedRows`, add `needs_mode_floor: { count: needsModeFloor, total: falseOfferTotal }` and `needsModeRows: needsModeRows.sort()`. Above the `needsMode` line, add a comment saying a head shows that label only when nothing else names a command, so a row counts only when neither the typed command nor the route delivered one, and a silent row that carries it shows a label nobody asked for. Then run `node $CAP --write`. The build still holds the old rule, which ignores the third argument, so this capture records the before rows. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":3,\"total\":35}`, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows | length' $BASE` prints 16, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[]' $BASE | rg -c '^(nm-sk-design-01|nm-sk-doc-01|nm-system-skill-advisor-01|cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01|cmd-create-repo-rule-plain-tune-01)$'` prints 5, `diff <(jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha, .attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows)' $BASE) <(git -c core.fsmonitor=false show HEAD:$BASE | jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha)')` prints nothing and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- [x] T003 [P] Report the rows whose head would read `(needs a mode)` and recapture the baseline (`CAP`, `BASE`). Add `const PROMPT_POLICY_MODULE = resolve(DIST, 'lib/prompt-policy.js')` beside `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE`, add it to the array the existence loop checks, import `extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions` from it after the `COMMAND_ATTACH_MODULE` import and add `routeNeedsMode` to that import's names. Before the corpus loop, declare `needsModeRows` as an empty array and `needsModeFloor` as 0. Inside the loop, hold the hub's route as `const route = topId !== undefined && COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS.has(topId) ? readCompiledRoute(workspaceRoot, topId, row.prompt) : undefined` and pass `route` to `attachCommand` where the call reads the route inline today, so the label reuses the same lookup. After the line that sets `delivered`, add `const needsMode = route !== undefined && delivered === undefined && routeNeedsMode(topId, route, extractMetalinguisticSkillMentions(row.prompt))` and push `row.id` into `needsModeRows` when it is true. Inside the `wantsSilence` block, add 1 to `needsModeFloor` when `needsMode` is true. In `attachedMetrics`, right after `attachedRows`, add `needs_mode_floor: { count: needsModeFloor, total: falseOfferTotal }` and `needsModeRows: needsModeRows.sort()`. Above the `needsMode` line, add a comment saying a head shows that label only when nothing else names a command, so a row counts only when neither the typed command nor the route delivered one, and a silent row that carries it shows a label nobody asked for. Then run `node $CAP --write`. The build still holds the old rule, which ignores the third argument, so this capture records the before rows. Verify: `node --check $CAP` exits 0, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":3,\"total\":35}`, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows | length' $BASE` prints 16, `jq -r '.attachedMetrics.needsModeRows[]' $BASE | rg -c '^(nm-sk-design-01|nm-sk-doc-01|nm-system-skill-advisor-01|cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01|cmd-create-repo-rule-plain-tune-01)$'` prints 5, `diff <(jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha, .attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows)' $BASE) <(git -c core.fsmonitor=false show HEAD:$BASE | jq -S 'del(.capturedAtSha)')` prints nothing and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '83p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794565987568,"end":1794565988887}}}}
